  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1019 PM CDT Sat May 9 2026\n\nThese meager amounts of rain are unfortunate. I say this because \nwhile we have low rain chances a couple of times over the next week \nto 10 days, rainfall amounts remain limited. The first chance is \nTuesday night into Wednesday and another next weekend. Currently, \nboth look pathetic and the bump we got from last week's rain may \nvery well be short-lived as drought conditions may only prove to \nbecome worse through at least the middle of the month. I suppose if \nthere's any good news, temperatures should remain tolerable with \nhighs near or only a few degrees above normal this week. There \nare some indications this could change in our extended guidance, \nbut I'll need to see that for a few more runs to start talking \nabout it at any great length. In the end, we can hang our hats on \nthe high likelihood of no severe weather any time soon.",
